  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "#Marcus Reyes — Visualization Supervisor\r\n\r\nMarcus plans complex film scenes digitally before they're shot. His workstation has a high-end graphics card, and he plays scenes back for the director to approve. Heavy scenes go over the studio network to render overnight.\r\n\r\n### What's Going Wrong?\r\n* Short playback is fine. Anything past a few seconds stutters.\r\n* Two overnight renders shut the machine off partway through.\r\n* It never happens on quick tasks — only on anything sustained.\r\n* It started about a month ago.",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true",
